                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3d136e6d-6bda-3036-9af3-12a0368f6997",
                                        "entry_id": "7da3423b-a475-32da-bc37-1325cb9166f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A round picture or other work of art."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0cf1097a-8def-42ae-9a9a-c2196bec9251",
                                                "sense_id": "3d136e6d-6bda-3036-9af3-12a0368f6997",
                                                "text": "As the ellipse becomes longer and flatter, it takes on the qualities of the rectangle. Even more than the tondo, the oval is a playful shape, prescribed by the demands of the setting it bedecks rather than those of the composition it encloses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d14c34d-6caa-4737-94ec-d8eb6846c125",
                                                "sense_id": "3d136e6d-6bda-3036-9af3-12a0368f6997",
                                                "text": "In the tondo of a cup in the Louvre we see a young slave, a pais, dip an oenochoe into a garlanded krater; he is holding a cup in the other hand and is about to serve drinks (fig. 20).” By isolating this detail, the painter implies all the aspects of a […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "889906e2-b77d-44f0-a5c7-26f9c92a13be",
